{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"14042ccccd8e738c2a074f55fa908eb7fa31e744cfba44cc3b9658057ffaf854","slug":"unit-09","location":"/Unit_09.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Unit 9","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3 (ipykernel)","language":"python"},"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Maite Taboada","given":"Maite","family":"Taboada"},"name":"Maite Taboada","id":"contributors-Maite\\MOD\\notebooks\\python_text_analysis\\myst-generated-uid-0"}],"binder":"https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/maitetaboada/python_text_analysis/main","copyright":"2025","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"Unit_09.ipynb","url":"/Unit_09-6e7e5bea067e6d37e5e6b005173c77e6.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sentiment analysis","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"wmIiVzJw8W"}],"identifier":"sentiment-analysis","label":"Sentiment analysis","html_id":"sentiment-analysis","implicit":true,"key":"Ico7BmZLYn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sentiment analysis is a computational method to extract ‘sentiment’ from text. What ‘sentiment’ means varies, but in general, it is the positive or negative opinion about something that is conveyed in the text.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ogJcjmbFfj"}],"key":"JkEbTtSzxr"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most basic methods have a dictionary of positive and negative words and then check to see how many of those are in the text in question. You can do fancy calculations, but a difference or relative proportio